Hi,

I have a problem with my Shiny dashboard. The user can upload a csv file, the first column containing terms they will search for on the database the dashboard connects to.

The table is passed to a function that will perform the query but it does not seem to be able to correctly read the column.

Here's my code. Its been changed here to create a table rather than search as an example. This code returns no rows in the created table.
dataTable <- reactive({
  if(is.null(input$uploadBox)){
    return(NULL)
  } else {
    dataTbl <- read.csv(input$uploadBox$datapath, stringsAsFactors = FALSE)

    return(as.data.table(dataTbl))
  }
})

searchFunc <- eventReactive(input$uploadButton, {
   source(paste0(currPath, "/pgm/dbConnection.r"))

   sqlSearch(dataTable())
})

sqlSearch <- function(data){
  sqlQuery(conn, stri_paste("drop table if exists ",my521,"_upload_search_names;"))
  sqlQuery(conn, stri_paste("create table if not exists ",my521,"_upload_search_names
                        (search_name varchar)
                        stored as parquet
                        ;"))

  for(i in 1:nrow(data)){
    sqlQuery(conn, stri_paste("insert into ",my521,"_upload_search_names
                               select
                               ",data[i,1],"
                               ;"))
  }
}

I have also tried changing the first column to a string with
searchVar <- toString(sprintf("'%s'", data[,1]))

and changing the for(i in 1:nrow(data)) to length(searchVar) and looping with searchVar[i] but all that does is insert one row containing "c('item1','item2','item3',... 'item33')"

I'm at a loss how to use the data table uploaded in the function that queries the database. When I use a test file I have on the Shiny server and run the sql functions manually everything works fine. So I'm thinking it has to do with how the data table is passed to the function.

Thank you for any help.

